+## 3. Assumptions for the gaps
+
+Each row is logged in `.context/deferrals/cd-1_deferral-register.md` under `## Assumptions`.
+
+| Gap | Assumption | Settled by |
+|---|---|---|
+| G-1 | "Where the money went" is the place of performance (`primary_place_of_performance_state_code` and the county FIPS column of the same place block, names verified in Phase 2). A foreign place of performance goes to state `FOREIGN` and county `FOREIGN`. A US place with no county FIPS goes to county `UNKNOWN` in its state. Every source row lands in exactly one bucket, so county, state and source totals reconcile exactly. The bucketing is in dbt staging. | Phase 2 (column names checked against the CSV header), Phase 3 (`stg_usaspending__transactions`, `dim_place`), Phase 4 (reconciliation test) |
+| G-2 | "Month" is the calendar month of `action_date`, labelled `YYYY-MM`. FY2024 rows are those with `action_date_fiscal_year = 2024`. The engine fails the batch run if an FY2024 row has an `action_date` outside 2023-10-01 to 2024-09-30. | Phase 2 (engine assertion), Phase 3 (filter and `dim_date`) |
+| G-3 | An award is one value of `generated_unique_award_id`, across the contract and assistance files. Check 3 counts awards whose summed FY2024 `federal_action_obligation` is below zero. A per-transaction count is not used. | Phase 3 (`dim_award` key), Phase 4 (check 3 view) |
+| G-4 | Per-person is FY2024 obligations (check 2) or monthly obligations (the monthly mart) divided by the county population for July 1, 2024 (`POPESTIMATE2024`). The monthly mart holds the monthly rate and says so in its column description. Population is a county attribute. It is never summed across agency rows. A state population is the sum of its county populations, with each county counted once. | Phase 3 (mart columns, uniqueness test on county population), Phase 4 (check 2) |
+| G-5 | Obligations are `DECIMAL(18,2)` in the lake and the marts. Per-person values are `DECIMAL(18,2)`, rounded half away from zero. Sums are on decimals only; no float cast anywhere, including the Polars and DataFusion steps. | Phase 2 (decimal parse, decimal test), Phase 3 (contract `data_type` on every money column) |
+| G-6 | Change types `edit` and `new` count as edits. `log` and `categorize` events are kept in `fct_edit` with their `change_type` and are not counted as edits. Lateness applies to every first arrival. A null `length.old` or `length.new` gives a 0 byte delta and `has_length = false`. Lateness is computed in the engine at ingest, because it needs stream history (see cd-1-late-classification). The edit fact keeps late events. The late events are also in `late_events`. | Phase 5 (classification, tests), Phase 6 (`fct_edit`, `late_events`, window filters) |
+| G-7 | The event identity for dedupe is `meta.id`. The consumer position (last SSE `id`) and the running maximum event time are stored in the footer of the micro-batch Parquet file. That file appears by one atomic `os.replace` from `_tmp/`. A restart reads the footer of the highest committed batch and reloads the set of committed `meta.id` values. | Phase 5 (sink and commit), Phase 5 crash tests |
+| G-8 | `make build` idempotence is checked by row content, sorted by the table key, with all columns compared. The lake and the marts carry no load timestamp and no run id. The lake keeps `_source_sha256` and `_source_file` only. A byte comparison is reported but not required. Each build replaces the batch table folders it owns, so no stale file remains. | Phase 2 (deterministic writes), Phase 7 (double-build integration test) |
+| G-9 | `make build` runs `dbt build --exclude tag:stream`. `make stream DURATION=<s>` runs the engine on `pipelines/stream.yml` with `--duration <s>`, then `dbt build --select tag:stream`. If the replay ends before DURATION, the engine exits 0 and the dbt step still runs. A missing DURATION makes `make stream` fail with a message. | Phase 6 (stream models), Phase 7 (Makefile, end-to-end run) |
+| G-10 | "The replayed hour" is the first UTC event-time hour in `fct_edit`: from `date_trunc('hour', min(event_time))` to that plus one hour, end exclusive, where `event_time` is the event `timestamp`. Check 5 counts every consumed edit in that hour, late or on time. The hour is recorded in `DECISIONS.md` with the value found. | Phase 6 (check 5 view and its test on the fixture), Phase 7 (value recorded in DECISIONS.md) |
+| G-11 | The stack sections are not in the snapshot. The stack is the set of pins in `pyproject.toml`, plus the stdlib SSE client (`urllib`). Output 3 "plus whatever the stack section asks for" is taken as: `Makefile`, `oracle_map.yml`, `DECISIONS.md`, `pipelines/`, `engine/`, `transform/`, and the published `out/marts/`. | Phase 1 (pins unchanged), Phase 7 (deliverable list checked) |
+| G-12 | A mart is a dbt model: SQL file under `transform/models/marts/`, a schema YAML entry with an enforced contract, and no Python. The engine YAML covers sources, ingestion transforms and sinks only. Marts are published by a folder config in `dbt_project.yml`, so a new mart needs no engine change. | Phase 3 (folder config, post-hook, exit check) |
+
+Non-blocking gaps, chosen and logged in `DECISIONS.md` (Phase 7):
+- N-1: The Census file is filtered to `SUMLEV = 050`. The join key is the 5-digit FIPS `STATE || COUNTY`, both zero-padded. The 2024 file is the primary source. Amendment A fallback: a county with no `POPESTIMATE2024` row uses the latest earlier estimate. That is `POPESTIMATE2021` from the 2021 file, since the 2024 file has no row for the eight old Connecticut counties. The fallback is named per county in DECISIONS.md. If a county is missing from both files, population is NULL and a dbt test reports the row. The fallback is not extended further.
+- N-2: The stream `wiki` field is the dbname (for example `enwiki`). It joins to `data/raw/sitematrix.json` by dbname, which gives language and project. Check 6 filters on `server_name = 'en.wikipedia.org'`, which maps 1:1 to `wiki = 'enwiki'` (a test asserts it). The bot field is `bot` (boolean).
+- N-3: The YAML format is JSON Schema (`engine/schema/pipeline.schema.json`, already in the skeleton). The `oracle_map.yml` format is a list of `{check, relation, columns, description}` rows (Phase 4).
+- N-4: The resume uses the `Last-Event-ID` request header, with the position stored in the batch footer.
+- N-5: Ties in check 6 are broken by `window_start` ascending. Check 6 lists the top 10 windows.
+- N-6: "Contract and grant money" is the union of the Contracts and Assistance files, in dbt staging. The fact key is `transaction_key`, which is the source file type prefixed to the source's own transaction key (`C:` or `A:`).
+- N-7: The event time is the `timestamp` field (integer epoch seconds). The ISO `meta.dt` is not used for windowing (see cd-1-event-time).
+- N-8: `dim_date` covers each calendar day from 2023-10-01 to 2024-09-30, the FY2024 window. The stream models use `window_start` and do not join `dim_date`.
