+## 5. Design decisions
+
+Each decision has a record in `.context/proposals/cd-1-<slug>.md`. Records marked (new) are written by this run; the others already exist and are kept as written. The engine-transforms record does not name the SQL steps, so Phase 2 names them (section 2).
+
+| Decision | Choice | Rejects |
+|---|---|---|
+| cd-1-lake-layout | One folder per lake table, Parquet, rows sorted by key, deterministic file names, `_source_sha256` and `_source_file` as the only load metadata | Load timestamp, run id, random file names |
+| cd-1-engine-transforms | `engine:` in each transform names `polars` or `datafusion`. Polars does row-wise steps (casts, decimal and date parsing, FIPS padding, sitematrix flattening). DataFusion does SQL steps (Census county filter and key) | One engine only |
+| cd-1-engine-schema | JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) checked with `jsonschema`. Error line numbers come from the PyYAML node tree (`yaml.compose`), so each error names file, line and problem | Pydantic, hand-written checks |
+| cd-1-stream-commit | The micro-batch is one Parquet file, written to `lake/stream_events/_tmp/`, then moved into `lake/stream_events/` by one `os.replace`. The footer holds `last_sse_id`, `max_event_time` and the batch id. The file is the commit | A separate position file (two writes, not atomic) |
+| cd-1-late-classification | The engine marks each first arrival as on time or late, using the running maximum event time from the last committed footer. Late is `max_prev > window_end + 10 min`, strictly. Dedupe on `meta.id`. The window mart reads on-time rows only | dbt-side classification (needs history across batches) |
+| cd-1-county-place | Place of performance, with buckets `FOREIGN` and `UNKNOWN` (see G-1), applied in dbt staging | Recipient county, dropping rows, bucketing in the lake |
+| cd-1-month-and-award | Calendar month of `action_date`; award key `generated_unique_award_id` | Fiscal month numbering; per-transaction counts |
+| cd-1-money-type | `DECIMAL(18,2)` everywhere; half-away-from-zero rounding on per-person | `DOUBLE` sums |
+| cd-1-per-person | July 1, 2024 population (`POPESTIMATE2024`), with the 2021 fallback per Amendment A; population not additive across agency rows | Census 2020 base (`CENSUS2020BASE`); summing population per agency |
+| cd-1-edit-types | Edits are `edit` and `new`; other types kept in the fact with their type | Counting every change event as an edit |
+| cd-1-window-incremental | Window mart is incremental with `delete+insert`, `unique_key` of window, wiki, namespace and actor type, and a lower bound from a state table (see the record) | Full rebuild each run (correct, but not incremental as the request asks) |
+| cd-1-mart-publish | Marts are `table` models with an enforced contract; a post-hook copies each to `out/marts/<mart>/<mart>.parquet` | dbt external materialization (no contract enforcement) |
+| cd-1-stream-replay-ids | Stream resume uses `Last-Event-ID`; the SSE reader is stdlib `urllib`, so no HTTP dependency is added | `requests` or `httpx` added as dependencies |
+| cd-1-mart-definition (new) | A mart is a dbt SQL model with a schema YAML contract. The engine YAML covers sources, transforms and sinks only | Marts as engine YAML entries (would duplicate dbt's contracts and lineage) |
+| cd-1-replay-hour (new) | "Replayed hour" is the first UTC event-time hour in `fct_edit`, end exclusive (see G-10) | Wall-clock hour of the consumer run; the whole lake |
+| cd-1-event-time (new) | Event time is `timestamp` (integer epoch seconds). `meta.dt` is not used for windows | `meta.dt` (ISO string, parsed per row, adds a second time source) |
+| cd-1-make-targets (new) | `make build` and `make stream` are the only targets. `build` is the batch engine run then `dbt build --exclude tag:stream`. `stream` is the engine run with `--duration` then `dbt build --select tag:stream` | New targets for each step (the request names two targets) |
+
+## 6. Decision records
+
+The records in `.context/proposals/cd-1-*.md` are the decision records for section 5. Each has the P1 frontmatter (`decision_id`, `status: proposed`, `question`, `choice`, `rationale`) and a `Ticket: cd-1` line. Phase 1 checks that each row of section 5 has a record file. P5 reads them for decision coverage.
