+### Phase 5: Stream source and the stream sink
+Scope:
+- Engine: the `sse` source kind, read with stdlib `urllib`. It parses `id:` and `data:` lines, sends `Last-Event-ID` on reconnect (N-4), and retries with a fixed backoff. The `--duration SECONDS` flag on `run` stops the source and flushes the buffer.
+- Late classification at ingest (cd-1-late-classification, G-6): a first arrival is late when its `window_end` plus 10 minutes is before the running maximum of `timestamp` over earlier first arrivals (strictly more than 10 minutes). The running maximum starts at the `max_event_time` in the last committed footer. A late first arrival still advances it. A redelivered `meta.id` is dropped and does not change the maximum.
+- Windows: `window_start = floor(timestamp / 300) * 300`, `window_end = window_start + 300`, both UTC epoch seconds.
+- Sink `parquet_stream`: a micro-batch is committed when it has N events or T seconds of data (both in YAML). The file is written to `lake/stream_events/_tmp/batch-<id>.parquet`, then moved to `lake/stream_events/batch-<id>.parquet` by `os.replace`. The footer holds `last_sse_id`, `max_event_time` and `batch_id`. Stop at DURATION flushes the buffer as a final batch. A buffer that is not committed is not counted (its SSE ids are re-read on restart).
+- Restart: read the footer of the highest committed batch, set `Last-Event-ID`, the running maximum and the batch counter. Reload the committed `meta.id` values for dedupe (G-7).
+- Fields kept per row: `meta_id`, `timestamp`, `wiki` (dbname), `server_name`, `namespace`, `type`, `bot`, `length_old`, `length_new` (nullable), `window_start`, `window_end`, `is_late`, `max_prev_event_time`, `batch_id`.
+TDD: a local fake SSE server in the test, with fixed events and ids, a disconnect after N events, a redelivery of an earlier id, and an exact-10-minute case (not late) and an 11-minute case (late). Crash tests: an exception raised after the `_tmp` write and before `os.replace` (the batch is not counted; on restart the events are read again and counted once), and an exception after `os.replace` (the batch is counted once).
+Exit: `uv run pytest engine/tests -k stream` passes. `uv run python -m engine run pipelines/stream.yml --duration 5` against the fake server gives the same set of `meta_id` values as one uninterrupted run over the same fixed events.
